-- 15  Chicken, Leek & Mushroom Pie
--     https://www.bbc.co.uk/food/recipes/chickenandmushroompi_89034
UPDATE `recipe` SET `method` = '1. Preheat the oven to 200C, 180C fan, or gas 6.
2. Heat the oil in a frying pan. Add the chicken and fry until it begins to turn white.
3. Add the mushrooms and continue frying until the chicken is golden-brown.
4. Remove the chicken and mushrooms from the pan and set aside. Add the onion and garlic to the same pan and fry for 2.5 minutes, or until softened. Remove from the heat and set aside with the chicken and mushrooms.
5. Melt the butter in a saucepan. Stir in the flour and cook for about 3 minutes, stirring constantly, until it forms a thick, smooth paste.
6. Mix the milk and stock in a jug, then add the nutmeg, white pepper and salt to taste. Slowly pour the liquid into the flour mixture, whisking constantly until smooth. Simmer over a gentle heat, stirring constantly, for about 5 minutes or until smooth and thickened.
7. Stir in the parsley and pour the sauce over the chicken and mushroom mixture. Mix well, then spoon into a pie dish and leave until completely cool.
8. If using a block of pastry, roll it out on a lightly floured surface until it is the thickness of a pound coin. Brush the edges of the pie dish with beaten egg, lay the pastry on top, press down the edges and trim. Brush the top with beaten egg and use leftover pastry to decorate if desired.
9. Make two or three slits in the top to allow steam to escape. Bake for 22.5 minutes, or until the pastry is golden-brown.'
WHERE `id` = 15
  AND `remote_url` = 'https://www.bbc.co.uk/food/recipes/chickenandmushroompi_89034'
  AND (`method` IS NULL OR TRIM(`method`) = '');

