-- 44  Fresh Egg Pasta
--     https://www.saltfatacidheat.com/fat/pasta-alluovo
UPDATE `recipe` SET `method` = '1. Mound the flour in the centre of a large, wide mixing bowl. Make a well in the centre and add the eggs and egg yolks. Using a fork, beat the eggs and gradually incorporate the flour from the inner rim of the well. Continue until about half the flour is incorporated and the dough forms a shaggy mass.
2. Use your fingers to mix the dough, pressing any loose flour into the dough. If needed, add another egg yolk or a tablespoon of water to absorb all the flour. Once cohesive, remove the dough from the bowl.
3. Transfer the dough to a lightly floured surface and knead for 4 to 5 minutes, until smooth, elastic and uniform in colour. Wrap in plastic and rest at room temperature for at least 30 minutes and up to 4 hours.
4. Line three baking sheets with parchment paper and lightly dust with semolina flour.
5. Cut off one quarter of the dough, rewrap the remainder and set it aside. Flatten the piece into an oval about the width of the pasta machine. Set the rollers to their widest setting and pass the dough through.
6. Lay the dough on a lightly floured work surface and fold it in half so it is again the width of the pasta machine. Pass it through the widest setting again. Continue folding the dough in thirds and rolling it until smooth, silky and even-textured, keeping the sheet as wide as the machine.
7. Roll the dough once through each of the next 2 to 3 settings, dusting with flour as needed, until it is about 1/4 inch thick.
8. From this point, roll the dough twice through each setting. Lightly dust both sides with flour as needed to prevent sticking. Continue until the pasta is thin enough to see the outline of your hand beneath it, about 1/16 inch thick for noodles.
9. Cut the pasta into sheets 12 to 14 inches long. Lightly dust with semolina flour, stack on a prepared baking sheet and cover with a clean, lightly damp kitchen towel. Repeat with the remaining dough.
10. For roller-cut noodles, pass each pasta sheet through the cutting attachment, then toss with semolina flour. Gently fluff and separate the noodles, form into single-portion nests, and place on the prepared baking sheets. Cover until ready to use.
11. For hand-cut noodles, stack four semolina-dusted pasta sheets and loosely fold them in thirds lengthwise. Cut with a sharp knife:
    - Cut in 1/2-inch increments for tagliatelle or fettuccine.
    - Cut in 3/4-inch increments for pappardelle.
12. Gently fluff and separate the noodles, form into single-portion nests on the prepared baking sheets, and cover until ready to use.'
WHERE `id` = 44
  AND `remote_url` = 'https://www.saltfatacidheat.com/fat/pasta-alluovo'
  AND (`method` IS NULL OR TRIM(`method`) = '');

