-- 49  Bagels
--     https://www.sophisticatedgourmet.com/2009/10/new-york-style-bagel-recipe/
UPDATE `recipe` SET `method` = '1. Pour the sugar and yeast into 120 millilitres of the warm water without stirring. Leave for 5 minutes, then stir until dissolved.
2. Mix the flour and salt in a large bowl. Make a well in the centre and add the yeast mixture.
3. Add 80 millilitres of warm water, then mix in the remaining water as needed to make a moist, firm dough. Add up to 60 millilitres more water if necessary.
4. Knead the dough on a floured work surface for about 10 minutes, until smooth and elastic. Work in as much flour as needed to make a firm, stiff dough.
5. Lightly oil a large bowl, add the dough and turn to coat. Cover with a damp towel and leave in a warm place for 1 hour, until doubled in size. Punch down the dough and rest for 10 minutes.
6. Divide the dough into 8 pieces. Shape each piece into a smooth round.
7. Press a floured finger through the centre of each dough ball to make a ring. Stretch each ring to form a bagel and place on a lightly oiled baking sheet.
8. Cover the shaped bagels with a damp towel and rest for 10 minutes. Meanwhile, preheat the oven to 220°C.
9. Bring a large pot of water to the boil, then reduce the heat. Lower in the bagels in batches. Once they float, boil for 1 minute, flip, and boil for 1 more minute. For chewier bagels, boil for 2 minutes on each side.
10. Add optional toppings as the bagels come out of the water. An egg wash may be used to help toppings stick.
11. Transfer the boiled bagels to an oiled or parchment-lined baking sheet.
12. Bake for 20 to 25 minutes, until golden brown.
13. Cool on a wire rack before serving.'
WHERE `id` = 49
  AND `remote_url` = 'https://www.sophisticatedgourmet.com/2009/10/new-york-style-bagel-recipe/'
  AND (`method` IS NULL OR TRIM(`method`) = '');

-- 50  Pizzas
--     https://anitalianinmykitchen.com/best-pizza-dough/
UPDATE `recipe` SET `method` = '1. Add the lukewarm water to the bowl of a stand mixer or a large bowl. Sprinkle over the sugar and yeast, leave for 5-10 minutes, then stir to combine.
2. For machine kneading, add the olive oil, flour and salt. Mix with the dough hook on low speed, scrape down the hook, then knead on medium speed for 5-7 minutes, scraping the hook halfway through, until the dough is smooth and elastic.
3. For hand kneading, add the olive oil, flour and salt and mix with a fork until the dough begins to come together. Turn out onto a lightly floured surface and knead for about 10 minutes, until smooth and elastic. Add a little extra flour if the dough is very sticky.
4. Place the dough in a lightly oiled bowl and turn it to coat. Cover with plastic wrap and a clean kitchen towel, then leave in a warm, draft-free place for about 2 hours, or until doubled in size.
5. Preheat the oven to 250°C. Punch down the dough, divide into 1-3 balls and leave to rest for 20 minutes.
6. Place the dough on lightly oiled pizza trays or baking sheets and shape it with clean hands.
7. Add your preferred toppings and bake for 15-20 minutes, until the crust is golden and the cheese has melted.
8. Alternatively, refrigerate the dough in an airtight plastic bag for up to 24 hours.
9. For a simple tomato sauce, combine a tin of diced or puréed tomatoes with oregano, basil, salt and olive oil, then spread over the pizza dough.
10. For a fresh tomato topping, chop grape, cherry or Roma tomatoes. Remove the seeds from Roma tomatoes, then toss with oregano, basil, salt and olive oil.
11. For a sausage topping, fry chopped Italian sausage until beginning to brown. Add sliced onion, pepper, mushrooms, olive oil, oregano, basil, salt and pepper, then cook over medium heat for about 10 minutes. Use as a pizza topping over the sauce before baking.'
WHERE `id` = 50
  AND `remote_url` = 'https://anitalianinmykitchen.com/best-pizza-dough/'
  AND (`method` IS NULL OR TRIM(`method`) = '');

