-- 55  Duck breast with cabbage, beetroot and sweet potato
--     https://www.greatbritishchefs.com/recipes/duck-breast-recipe-lavender-beetroot-sweet-potato
UPDATE `recipe` SET `method` = '1. Toast the szechuan pepper, coriander seeds, cumin seeds and fennel seeds in a dry pan over medium heat for 5 minutes.
2. Roughly crush the toasted spices using a mortar and pestle. Mix with the lavender and set aside.
3. Preheat the oven to 190°C, gas mark 5. Cover the beetroot with foil and roast until tender, about 37.5 minutes. Allow to cool slightly, peel while still warm, then cut into large cubes.
4. Dice the sweet potato, season with salt and coat with olive oil. Place on a baking tray and roast until tender, about 40 minutes, alongside the beetroot.
5. Heat a large dry pan over medium-high heat. Season the duck breasts with salt and place them skin-side down in the pan. Slowly render the fat, carefully spooning off excess fat as it is released.
6. Cook the duck for 6 minutes, then turn and cook for a further 4 minutes. Finish in the oven at 220°C, gas mark 6, for 2 minutes. Rest for 6 minutes.
7. Press the flesh side of the rested duck breasts into the spice and lavender mixture.
8. Heat a second pan over medium-high heat. Add butter and, once foaming, add the roasted beetroot and sweet potato. Heat through, season with salt, then remove from the heat.
9. Return the duck to the pan, flesh-side down, and sear the spices for 1 minute. Add the maple syrup and coat the duck until reduced to a sticky glaze. Slice and serve over the roasted vegetables.'
