-- 89  Porchetta w/ Salsa Verde
--     https://basicswithbabish.co/basicsepisodes/porchetta
UPDATE `recipe` SET `method` = '1. Remove the skin from the portion of pork belly that will be inside the roll.
2. Score the meat inside the belly in both directions, making cuts about 5 cm apart and 2.5 cm deep to create a crosshatch pattern.
3. Trim the pork belly into a neat rectangle.
4. Season the meat with nutmeg, orange zest, sage, rosemary, fennel fronds or fennel seeds, pine nuts, chilli flakes, and crushed garlic. Press the seasonings into the scored cuts.
5. Roll the pork belly tightly. Make shallow lateral cuts through the skin, ensuring they do not reach the fat.
6. Tie the roast with butcher''s twine every 2.5 to 7.5 cm.
7. Place the roast on a wire rack over a baking sheet and refrigerate uncovered overnight.
8. Line the baking sheet with foil, return the rack and roast to the tray, and heat the oven to 250°F. Insert a temperature probe into the thickest part of the roast.
9. Roast for 3 to 8 hours, until the internal temperature reaches 160°F.
10. Remove the roast carefully, as there will be a large amount of rendered fat.
11. Increase the oven temperature to 500°F. Return the roast to the oven and watch closely until the skin is crisp without burning.
12. Rest for 30 minutes before slicing.
13. To make the salsa verde, combine parsley, lemon zest and juice, capers, white wine vinegar, anchovies, garlic, olive oil, and chilli flakes in a food processor or immersion blender bowl. Blend until chopped but still textured.
14. Season the salsa verde to taste with salt and pepper.
15. For sandwiches, layer thinly sliced porchetta on focaccia, spread with salsa verde, top with arugula, then secure with skewers, slice, and serve.'
