-- 300117  Slow-cooked Beef Stroganoff
--     https://simplehomeedit.com/recipe/slow-cooked-beef-stroganoff/
UPDATE `recipe` SET `method` = '1. Season the beef with salt and pepper.
2. Heat 1 tablespoon olive oil in a large, deep, heavy-based pan over medium-high heat. Brown the beef in batches for 2-3 minutes on each side, adding the remaining oil as needed. Set aside.
3. Add 60 millilitres water to the pan and scrape up the browned bits. When most of the water has evaporated, add the onion and garlic and cook, stirring, for 2-3 minutes until softened.
4. Add the mushrooms and cook for 2-3 minutes until softened.
5. Add the flour and stir continuously for 30 seconds, until a paste forms around the onion and mushrooms.
6. Choose a cooking method:
   - Slow cooker: Add the tomato paste, paprika, Worcestershire sauce and beef stock to the slow cooker. Add the beef and mushroom mixture, then cook on high for 4 hours or low for 8 hours.
   - Pressure cooker: Add the tomato paste, paprika, Worcestershire sauce and beef stock to the pressure cooker insert. Return the beef and mushroom mixture, secure the lid, and cook on high pressure for 35 minutes. Let pressure release naturally for 10 minutes, then release any remaining pressure.
   - Stovetop: Add the tomato paste, paprika, Worcestershire sauce and beef stock to the pan, then return the beef. Bring to the boil, cover, and simmer over the lowest heat for 1.5 hours, stirring occasionally. Remove the lid and cook for 1 additional hour to thicken.
7. Check that the beef pulls apart easily with a fork. Continue cooking in short intervals if needed until tender.
8. Ladle about 250 millilitres sauce into a small bowl. Mix in the sour cream, then return the mixture to the cooker or pan and stir to combine.
9. If desired, reduce the sauce uncovered for 5-10 minutes, stirring occasionally, until thickened. Add up to 125 millilitres water if the stovetop sauce is sticking.
10. Serve with pasta, rice, polenta or mashed potato, garnished with parsley if using.'
